## Description
**Join COLIBRIX ONE – Innovating the Future of Payments**
At **COLIBRIX ONE\***, we’re building advanced, AI-powered payment technologies that support Payment Service Providers (PSPs), Electronic Money Institutions (EMIs), and neobanks across the EU and the UK. As a fully licensed Electronic Money Institution (FCA Reference No. 927920) and holder of a Financial Institution Licence issued by the MFSA, as well as a principal member of both VISA and Mastercard, we provide comprehensive, real-world financial solutions that include:
* Global card processing
* Digital wallet infrastructure
* Cross-border merchant accounts
* Alternative payment methods (APMs)
* Corporate accounts for legal entities
We’re a fast-growing team with a passion for innovation, security, and scalability. Our culture values curiosity, collaboration, and impact - and we’re looking for talented professionals who are ready to shape the future of fintech.
At COLIBRIX ONE, your work directly powers the digital economy. If you're eager to solve meaningful challenges and build with purpose, we’d love to hear from you.
**About The Role**
We're looking for a Product Owner to take ownership of core banking-related product capabilities and drive their evolution across our global product portfolio. This role sits at the intersection of product strategy, technology, and financial services, working closely with engineering teams, solution architects, and international stakeholders to deliver scalable digital banking solutions.
You'll play a key role in shaping the roadmap for mission-critical banking infrastructure used by financial institutions worldwide.
**Responsibilities**
* Own and drive the product vision, roadmap, and lifecycle for core banking-related products;
* Translate business requirements and market needs into clear product specifications and development priorities;
* Collaborate closely with engineering teams to ensure timely delivery of scalable and secure banking solutions;
* Manage and prioritize the product backlog, ensuring alignment with strategic objectives;
* Work with stakeholders across product, engineering, and business teams to define product features and enhancements;
* Analyze market trends, regulatory developments, and competitor solutions in digital banking and payments;
* Support global implementation projects by ensuring product capabilities meet client requirements;
* Drive continuous improvement of product performance, scalability, and user experience;
* Coordinate cross-team collaboration between product management, architecture, and delivery teams;
* Contribute to long-term product strategy across the company’s banking and payment platform ecosystem.
**What you need to succeed in this role**
* 3+ years of experience in Product Owner, Product Manager, or similar product leadership roles;
* Strong understanding of digital banking, payment platforms, or financial services technology;
* Ability to translate complex business and regulatory requirements into technical product features;
* Strong knowledge of EU regulations, including DORA and PSD2(3);
* Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills;
* Excellent stakeholder communication and cross-functional collaboration abilities;
* Experience working in international or multi-market technology environments;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and Russian
**What we offer**
* Opportunity to shape the future of fintech solutions within a growing company
* Collaborative, horizontal team structure that values your expertise and ideas
* Continuous learning and development opportunities to enhance your skills and career growth
* Competitive salary and benefits package
*\* This position is offered within the COLIBRIX ONE. Employment will be under the appropriate legal entity based on the role and location.*

# Digital Transformation Engineer
Digital Transformation Engineer
£36,000 to £40,000 pa
We are seeking a driven and detail-oriented Digital Transformation Engineer to support the delivery and ongoing management of our digital platforms and systems.
This role plays a key part in shaping and improving our technology landscape, working across the full product lifecycle from discovery and design through to release and continuous improvement. You’ll collaborate with stakeholders, technical teams, and external partners to deliver secure, reliable, and user-focused solutions.
**A full job description is available on request.**
What you will be doing as a Digital Transformation Engineer
* Support the end-to-end lifecycle of digital products, from planning through to release and optimisation;
* Monitor platform performance, troubleshoot issues, and support incident resolution;
* Ensure solutions meet quality, compliance, and user acceptance standards;
* Deliver training materials, user guides, and system documentation;
* Ensure compliance with GDPR and company data security standards;
* Maintain secure handling of system credentials and sensitive data.
What we need from you as a Digital Transformation Engineer
* Experience supporting digital or systems-based projects;
* Understanding of the software development lifecycle;
* Strong working knowledge of **Jira** and task management tools;
* Awareness of APIs, integrations, and data structures;
* Experience translating business requirements into technical deliverables;
* Strong attention to detail with the ability to manage multiple priorities.
What CSP can offer you as a Digital Transformation Engineer
* A competitive salary;
* A 37.5 hour working week;
* Up to 25 days’ holiday (pro-rata – after qualifying service) plus Bank/Public Holidays;
* Pension scheme with excellent employer contribution;
* Private Medical Insurance (after a qualifying period);
* Life insurance at 4x salary;
* Access to salary sacrifice schemes;
* A range of valuable medical and practical support services through an external Employee Assistance provider.
About CSP
CSP stands for The Combined Services Provider. It also stands for Caring, Safe, Professional, representing our Values. We specialise in providing services to venues and static sites including Car Parking, Internal and External Traffic Management, HVM (Hostile Vehicle Mitigation) solutions, Security, Stewarding, Cash & Audit and Consultancy services. Whilst our range of services has grown, Car Parking/Traffic Management, HVM, and Security/Stewarding represent our core areas of expertise.
CSP strives to be an equal opportunities employer.
